00:49:52.900 --> 00:49:56.380
You and I have talked about this, but I don't think we've ever talked about it on the pod.

1012
00:49:56.540 --> 00:49:57.260
So this is great.

1013
00:49:57.480 --> 00:50:00.480
I love that he had the same observation.

1014
00:50:01.220 --> 00:50:03.180
Okay, we'll play it and then we'll talk about it.

1015
00:50:03.480 --> 00:50:05.040
So this was a new experience for me.

1016
00:50:05.180 --> 00:50:07.500
I kind of, it was my first time being really on the set.

1017
00:50:07.760 --> 00:50:10.480
And I'm sitting in my trailer going, well, what do I do now?

1018
00:50:10.580 --> 00:50:11.700
So I decided to get something to eat.

1019
00:50:12.020 --> 00:50:14.520
I walk out and I'm like, where can I get some food?

1020
00:50:14.560 --> 00:50:16.860
And they pointed me in the direction of where the breakfast was.

1021
00:50:16.860 --> 00:50:21.500
And as I started walking, I heard someone in the headset go, cool guy, Paul's going to breakfaSt.

1022
00:50:21.960 --> 00:50:24.860
And then I come back and I hear them go, cool guy, Paul's back in his trailer.

1023
00:50:25.360 --> 00:50:27.660
Everywhere I went, someone's like, cool guy, Paul's in the bathroom.

1024
00:50:28.180 --> 00:50:29.040
Cool guy, Paul's in it.

1025
00:50:29.240 --> 00:50:31.060
Like someone had to know where I was at all times.

1026
00:50:31.160 --> 00:50:31.860
I thought it was really funny.

1027
00:50:31.980 --> 00:50:35.100
They had to track me to make sure they knew where I was in case they needed me.

1028
00:50:35.360 --> 00:50:38.740
So that was one super funny story from being on the set.

1029
00:50:38.740 --> 00:50:47.380
Yeah, you guys, on film and television sets, there is a whole network of production assistants

1030
00:50:47.380 --> 00:50:52.380
that wear these walkie-talkies and they have little earpieces, kind of like the Secret Service,

1031
00:50:52.640 --> 00:50:53.140
you know?

1032
00:50:53.300 --> 00:50:54.660
But not as fancy.

1033
00:50:54.920 --> 00:50:55.880
But not as fancy.

1034
00:50:56.040 --> 00:50:58.300
Like when they talk into them, you hear it echo.

1035
00:51:00.380 --> 00:51:04.980
Well, their job is literally to keep track of all the actors at all times.

1036
00:51:05.360 --> 00:51:09.920
And you can hear them tracking you all day as you walk by.

1037
00:51:10.180 --> 00:51:11.180
As you walk by.

1038
00:51:11.320 --> 00:51:15.780
And sometimes you hear it from the person directly behind you who's actually speaking about you.

1039
00:51:15.920 --> 00:51:21.220
And then you hear it in stereo from the other person they're talking to as you walk past them.

1040
00:51:21.360 --> 00:51:25.340
And I guess the theory behind it, Jenna, is that production needs to know where we are

1041
00:51:25.340 --> 00:51:29.480
because if the scene is lit and ready, they need us on that soundstage ready to go.

1042
00:51:29.640 --> 00:51:34.480
And they can't have an actor unaccounted for because then that holds everyone up and it costs money, right?

1043
00:51:34.780 --> 00:51:35.040
Yeah.

1044
00:51:35.160 --> 00:51:37.860
So when they're lighting a scene, they let you go back to your trailer.

1045
00:51:38.220 --> 00:51:39.240
You might use the restroom.

1046
00:51:39.340 --> 00:51:40.200
You might get a snack.

1047
00:51:40.360 --> 00:51:44.040
In our case, maybe we pop over to the writer's building and we're hanging out.

1048
00:51:44.340 --> 00:51:47.920
But once the scene is ready, they have no time to lose.

1049
00:51:48.380 --> 00:51:52.100
Because a production day is very regimented.

1050
00:51:52.100 --> 00:51:55.660
And if you run out of time, that means you probably have to cut something.

1051
00:51:56.120 --> 00:51:57.880
And you don't want that, right?

1052
00:51:58.020 --> 00:51:59.740
You don't want to have to cut content.

1053
00:52:00.180 --> 00:52:00.340
Right.

1054
00:52:00.520 --> 00:52:02.720
So, yeah, all day long.

1055
00:52:02.980 --> 00:52:08.280
But my favorite thing, Angela, is that they came up with a code for the bathroom.

1056
00:52:08.280 --> 00:52:11.900
I guess maybe it's to be, I don't know, more discreet.

1057
00:52:12.100 --> 00:52:14.240
But everyone knows what the code is.

1058
00:52:14.340 --> 00:52:16.080
The code is 10-1.

1059
00:52:16.780 --> 00:52:17.780
Jenna is 10-1.

1060
00:52:17.780 --> 00:52:20.980
Everyone knows when you go to the bathroom on a set.

1061
00:52:21.700 --> 00:52:23.160
Every single person.

1062
00:52:23.160 --> 00:52:25.880
It goes through every walkie-talkie.

1063
00:52:26.400 --> 00:52:27.260
Angela 10-1.

1064
00:52:27.540 --> 00:52:28.220
Jenna 10-1.

1065
00:52:28.740 --> 00:52:31.940
And I just want you to know, what if you need to 10-2?

1066
00:52:32.920 --> 00:52:34.660
And you're going to be in there for a minute.

1067
00:52:34.980 --> 00:52:40.900
Every time they would announce Jenna is 10-1, I would get a lot of anxiety because I would

1068
00:52:40.900 --> 00:52:43.620
think I better make it fast or they're going to think I'm doing a poop.

1069
00:52:44.040 --> 00:52:44.460
Right.

1070
00:52:44.460 --> 00:52:46.900
What about when we both started pumping?

1071
00:52:47.300 --> 00:52:49.680
And then you would hear in the walkie, Angela's pumping.

1072
00:52:50.060 --> 00:52:51.140
Angela's going to pump.

1073
00:52:51.540 --> 00:52:52.020
Yeah.

1074
00:52:52.200 --> 00:52:53.340
All your business.

1075
00:52:53.600 --> 00:52:56.100
All your business through a walkie-talkie.

1076
00:52:56.300 --> 00:52:57.500
It's crazy.

1077
00:52:57.720 --> 00:53:00.500
And I get why they have to do it, but it is very surreal.

1078
00:53:00.740 --> 00:53:05.520
And so that clip from Paul really, Jenna and I immediately called each other.

1079
00:53:05.660 --> 00:53:06.420
We're like, oh my gosh.

1080
00:53:06.820 --> 00:53:09.200
He talked about the thingy with the tracking.

1081
00:53:09.560 --> 00:53:10.080
The tracking.

1082
00:53:11.540 --> 00:53:14.120
They should warn you in film school.

1083
00:53:14.380 --> 00:53:16.320
That you're going to be tracked all day.

1084
00:53:16.460 --> 00:53:19.100
They should warn you because it's very jarring at firSt.

1085
00:53:19.360 --> 00:53:19.560
Yeah.

